# Flutter — SingleChildScrollView

## 1. What is `SingleChildScrollView`?

`SingleChildScrollView` makes a **single child scrollable**.

For example, if a form contains many fields and doesn't fit on a small phone screen, the user can scroll.

```dart
SingleChildScrollView(
  child: Column(
    children: [
      Text("Name"),
      Text("Email"),
      Text("Password"),
      Text("Phone"),
      Text("Address"),
    ],
  ),
)
```

---

# 2. Why Do We Need It?

Without scrolling:

```text
┌───────────────┐
│ Name          │
│ Email         │
│ Password      │
│ Phone         │
│ Address       │
│               │
│   OVERFLOW ↓  │
└───────────────┘
```

With `SingleChildScrollView`:

```text
┌───────────────┐
│ Name          │
│ Email         │
│ Password      │
│ Phone         │
│      ↓        │
│    Scroll     │
└───────────────┘
```

---

# 3. Most Common Use — Form

A very common pattern:

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: SingleChildScrollView(
    padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),

    child: Column(
      children: [

        TextFormField(
          decoration: InputDecoration(
            labelText: "Name",
            border: OutlineInputBorder(),
          ),
        ),

        SizedBox(height: 20),

        TextFormField(
          decoration: InputDecoration(
            labelText: "Email",
            border: OutlineInputBorder(),
          ),
        ),

        SizedBox(height: 20),

        TextFormField(
          decoration: InputDecoration(
            labelText: "Password",
            border: OutlineInputBorder(),
          ),
        ),

        SizedBox(height: 20),

        ElevatedButton(
          onPressed: () {},
          child: Text("Register"),
        ),
      ],
    ),
  ),
)
```

This is useful when the keyboard opens too and reduces the available screen space.

---

# 4. `SingleChildScrollView` + Form

You can combine it with the `Form` you just learned:

```dart
Form(
  key: formKey,

  child: SingleChildScrollView(
    child: Column(
      children: [

        TextFormField(),

        TextFormField(),

        TextFormField(),

        ElevatedButton(
          onPressed: () {
            if (formKey.currentState!.validate()) {
              print("Valid");
            }
          },
          child: Text("Submit"),
        ),

      ],
    ),
  ),
)
```

A common structure is:

```text
Form
 ↓
SingleChildScrollView
 ↓
Column
 ↓
TextFormFields
 ↓
Button
```

---

# 5. Padding

You can directly give padding:

```dart
SingleChildScrollView(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),

  child: Column(
    children: [
      Text("Hello"),
    ],
  ),
)
```

This is convenient instead of:

```dart
Padding(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),
  child: SingleChildScrollView(
    child: ...
  ),
)
```

Both can work.

---

# 6. Horizontal Scrolling

By default, it scrolls vertically.

You can change the direction:

```dart
SingleChildScrollView(
  scrollDirection: Axis.horizontal,

  child: Row(
    children: [
      Container(width: 200),
      Container(width: 200),
      Container(width: 200),
      Container(width: 200),
    ],
  ),
)
```

Result:

```text
┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐
│  1   │ │  2   │ │  3   │ │  4   │ →
└──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘
```

Useful for:

* Categories
* Horizontal cards
* Image galleries
* Tags

